# Environment variables for local development and deployment.
# Copy to .env.local and fill in values. Never commit .env.local.

# ── Voice Agent demo (ElevenLabs Conversational AI) ──────────────────────────
# Required for the live browser demo on /voice-agent.
# Create an agent in the ElevenLabs dashboard, then paste:
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID=

# Without both values, the page and API show "Demo currently unavailable"
# and never simulate a successful connection.

# ── Contact / project enquiry (Resend) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Required for POST /api/contact to accept enquiries for real delivery.
# Create an API key at https://resend.com and verify the from-domain.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Authenticated sender supported by Resend (not the visitor’s address), e.g.:
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=Buildaze <hello@your-verified-domain.com>
CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=
# Canonical recipient — must be team@buildaze.com.
# The server always delivers to team@buildaze.com; a different value here is ignored
# so an outdated env cannot silently redirect inquiries.
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=team@buildaze.com

# Optional safe test mode: accept submissions without sending real email.
# CONTACT_EMAIL_TRANSPORT=mock

# Without RESEND_API_KEY + CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL (and without mock transport),
# forms return an honest unconfigured error. Mailto drafts are a human fallback
# only — never counted as a received enquiry.
# Never put these secrets in client code or NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables.
# Do not send test inquiries to production inboxes without authorization.
# Run: npm run verify:contact
